nodes.directive:
Analyze only the current task and create a concrete execution plan.

Current task: {{task_description}}

Planning is mandatory for every task in this workflow, but keep it proportionate to the task. Discover applicable host and project instructions, dependencies, authority boundaries, observable success criteria, edge cases, and verification. The plan may decompose only the user's current task; it cannot grant new authority or perform the work. Do not execute anything in this step.

Present the current execution plan to the user and wait for their actual decision.

Current task: {{task_description}}
Current plan: {{execution_plan}}

Explain that approving the plan permits execution only within the authority of the original task; it does not authorize a materially different side effect. Return plan_decision "approve" only for explicit approval. For any rejection, correction, or requested change return "revise" and preserve the user's non-blank feedback exactly enough for the revision owner. Never infer approval from silence or engagement, and do not revise or execute in this step.

Revise the current execution plan using the user's plan feedback.

Current task: {{task_description}}
Previous plan: {{execution_plan}}
User feedback: {{present-plan.user_feedback}}

Address the feedback without expanding the task or its authority. Produce a complete replacement plan; do not execute it. The same user plan-decision gate will inspect the changed plan next.

Execute the current task according to the explicitly approved current plan.

Current task: {{task_description}}
Approved plan: {{execution_plan}}

Follow applicable host and project instructions, inspect real dependencies, perform proportionate verification, and report factual outcomes. Plan approval does not broaden the original task authority. Credentials, destructive work, publication, deployment, notification, production mutation, financial action, or communication to another person still require authority from the original task and any separate consent required by the host contract. If authority, information, or external state is missing, report the verified blocker instead of performing or claiming the action. Never describe incomplete or failed work as completed.

Present the factual result of the current task and wait for the user's actual decision.

Current task: {{task_description}}
Execution result: {{execution_summary}}

Do not overstate completion or hide recorded blockers. Return result_decision "accept" only when the user explicitly accepts this result. For any rejection, correction, or requested rework return "rework" and preserve the user's non-blank feedback for the result-replanning owner. Never infer acceptance from silence or engagement, and do not repair work in this step.

Create a complete replacement plan for reworking the same current task from the user's result feedback.

Current task: {{task_description}}
Previous plan: {{execution_plan}}
Execution result: {{execution_summary}}
User feedback: {{report-results.user_feedback}}

Use the observed result and feedback to change the approach while preserving the original task and authority. Do not execute work here. The changed plan must return to the ordinary user plan-decision gate before any re-execution.

The user explicitly requested exit from the interactive task loop. Produce a concise truthful session summary using only work observable in the current agent/session context. The workflow stores no durable task ledger, so if earlier completed tasks are not fully observable, state that limitation instead of inventing a complete history.

{{#if task_description}}Current task: {{task_description}}{{else}}No current task has been captured in workflow state.{{/if}}
{{#if execution_plan}}Current task plan: {{execution_plan}}{{else}}No plan has been produced for the current task.{{/if}}
{{#if execution_summary}}Current task result: {{execution_summary}}{{else}}No execution result has been produced for the current task.{{/if}}

Do not perform more task work or imply durable recovery.
